## Rate Limiting

### Redis Sliding Window Algorithm

Use sliding window over fixed window to prevent burst exploitation at window boundaries.

**Go implementation pattern (using Redis):**

```go
// internal/repository/redis/rate-limit/rate-limit.go
// Key: rate_limit:<identifier>:<window_start_unix>
// Algorithm:
// 1. ZADD key <current_timestamp_ms> <current_timestamp_ms>
// 2. ZREMRANGEBYSCORE key 0 <window_start_ms>  (remove old entries)
// 3. ZCARD key  (count requests in window)
// 4. If count > limit: reject (HTTP 429)
// 5. EXPIRE key <window_seconds>
```

**Rate Limit Tiers:**

| Endpoint Category | Limit | Window | Identifier |
|---|---|---|---|
| Auth (login, register) | 5 req | 1 minute | IP |
| OTP send | 3 req | 5 minutes | phone/email |
| OTP verify | 5 attempts | 10 minutes | phone/email |
| General API (authenticated) | 1000 req | 1 minute | user_id |
| General API (unauthenticated) | 60 req | 1 minute | IP |
| File upload | 10 req | 1 hour | user_id |

**Response Headers (always include):**
```
X-RateLimit-Limit: 100
X-RateLimit-Remaining: 87
X-RateLimit-Reset: 1716900000
Retry-After: 60  (only on 429)
```

