## CORS

- Restrict `Access-Control-Allow-Origin` to known origins in production.
- Do not use `*` in production without explicit justification.
- Allowlist origins from config/environment, not hardcoded.

```go
e.Use(middleware.CORSWithConfig(middleware.CORSConfig{
    AllowOrigins: config.Get().AllowedOrigins, // from environment
    AllowMethods: []string{"GET", "POST", "PUT", "DELETE", "OPTIONS"},
    AllowHeaders: []string{"Authorization", "Content-Type", "X-Request-ID"},
    MaxAge:       86400,
}))
```

---

## HTTPS / TLS

- Always use HTTPS in staging and production.
- Do not disable TLS verification in production code (`InsecureSkipVerify: false`).
- Use TLS 1.2 minimum; prefer TLS 1.3.

